msgid ""
"**Acropolis has reached end-of-life on September 2019. This page exists for "
"archival purposes. Please refer to the latest supported version.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:5
msgid "ROS Integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:7
msgid ""
"Most of the Gazebo libraries use [Gazebo Transport](https://github.com/"
"gazebosim/gz-transport) to exchange data between different software "
"components. This tutorial details how to interface with [ROS](http://www.ros."
"org/), enabling the ability to use tools such as [Rviz](http://wiki.ros.org/"
"rviz) for robot or sensor visualization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:13
msgid "ros1_gz_bridge to the rescue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:15
msgid ""
"ros1_gz_bridge provides a network bridge which enables the exchange of "
"messages between ROS 1 and Gazebo Transport. Its support is limited to only "
"certain message types. Please, read this [README](https://github.com/osrf/"
"ros1_ign_bridge) to verify if your message type is supported by the bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:20
msgid "How to install ros1_gz_bridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:22
msgid "Binary install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:24
msgid "Not available yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:26
msgid "Source install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:28
msgid ""
"See the [prerequisites](https://github.com/osrf/"
"ros1_ign_bridge#prerequisites) and [install section](https://github.com/osrf/"
"ros1_ign_bridge#building-the-bridge-from-source) of the bridge "
"documentation. This tutorial requires Ubuntu Melodic or newer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:32
msgid ""
"Assuming that you have ROS Melodic, you can install all dependencies with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:34
msgid ""
"sudo apt install ros-melodic-desktop ros-melodic-rqt-image-view libignition-"
"common3-dev libignition-transport6-dev\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:38
msgid "Run the bridge and exchange images"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:40
msgid ""
"In this example, we're going to generate Gazebo Transport images using "
"Gazebo, that will be converted into ROS 1 images, and visualized with "
"rqt_viewer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:42
msgid "First we start a ROS 1 `roscore`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:44
msgid ""
"# Shell A:\n"
". /opt/ros/melodic/setup.bash\n"
"roscore\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:50
msgid "Then we start Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:52
msgid ""
"# Shell B:\n"
"gz sim -r -f camera_sensor.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:57
msgid ""
"Gazebo should be running and publishing images over the `/camera` topic. "
"Let's verify it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:60
msgid ""
"# Shell C:\n"
"gz topic -l | grep \"^/camera\"\n"
"/camera\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:66
msgid "Then we start the parameter bridge with the previous topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:68
msgid ""
"# Shell D:\n"
". ~/bridge_ws/install/setup.bash\n"
"rosrun ros1_gz_bridge parameter_bridge /camera@sensor_msgs/Image@ignition."
"msgs.Image\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:74
msgid "Now we start the ROS 1 GUI:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:76
msgid ""
"# Shell E:\n"
". /opt/ros/melodic/setup.bash\n"
"rqt_image_view /camera\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_integration.md:82
msgid ""
"You should see the current images in `rqt_image_view` which are coming from "
"Gazebo (published as Gazebo Msgs over Gazebo Transport)."
msgstr ""

